  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction of HIV in Swaziland - Eswatini (01-Oct-2015-30-Sep-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini, HIV, Coordinating Assembly of Non Governmental Organisation (CANGO)This program has the following goals: Ensuring adequate health systems to support the attainment of health service targets, especially relating to HIV/AIDS, TB and Malaria.  Halt the spread of HIV and reverse its impact in Swazi society. The objectives of this program are: HIV - 50% reduction of new HIV infections among adults by 2015.  HIV - alleviate the socio-economic impacts of HIV and AIDS among vulnerable groups and across the population in general.  HIV - avert 15% deaths amongst PLHIV and in particular those with TB/HIV co-infection.  HIV - improve efficiency and effectiveness of the national response.  HIV - reduction of proportion of young people 15 - 24 who are living with HIV from 6% to 2% for men and from 23% to 10% for women by 2018 respectively</narrative>
  </description>
